Use mbedtls_md5() instead of the removed mbedtls_md5_ret()

mbedTLS 3.x dropped the _ret-suffixed digest entry points. The symbol is gone
from both the header and the library, so this is not a diagnostic that can be
suppressed -- with the warning demoted the build still fails at link:

  md5.c:66:5: error: implicit declaration of function 'mbedtls_md5_ret';
      did you mean 'mbedtls_md5_free'? [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]

Confirmed against the sysroot: mbedtls/md5.h declares mbedtls_md5_starts,
_update, _finish, mbedtls_md5 and _self_test, and libmbedcrypto.so.3.6.6
exports only those plus _init/_free/_clone. There is no mbedtls_md5_ret.

mbedtls_md5() is the direct replacement with the same signature and return
convention. The cast is needed because src is 'const char *' while the
prototype takes 'const unsigned char *'.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/libs/util/c/src/md5.c
+++ b/libs/util/c/src/md5.c
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@
 {
     unsigned char checksum[DIGEST_BYTE_LEN];
 
-    mbedtls_md5_ret(src, strlen(src), checksum);
+    mbedtls_md5((const unsigned char *) src, strlen(src), checksum);
 
     // now convert to string
     //
